[12.859132, "o", "\u001b[2mcollecting evidence from testbed and assessing with the model ...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[49.766128, "o", "\u001b[1m== testbed | problem | problem_key=ORA 600 [autodiag_repeat] | 2026-09-24 18:09:07 UTC\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[49.902926, "o", "\u001b[2m   model autodiag/qwen3.8-27b:32k, proofs 6/6 verified, confidence 85%, 34s, case case_ec8c0a1d63\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[50.048448, "o", "\r\n"]
[50.115534, "o", "\u001b[33m\u001b[1mWARNING:\u001b[0m Three identical ORA-00600 [autodiag_repeat] incidents occurred during instance startup, triggered by the `dbkeTest` kernel test flow; this is likely a diagnostic probe or test artifact rather than production corruption, but the identical call stack requires verification against the current Release Update.\r\r\n"]
[52.936321, "o", "\r\r\n"]
[54.805001, "o", "\u001b[1mConcerns:\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[54.879596, "o", " 1. \u001b[33m[warning/root_cause]\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRecurring ORA-00600 [autodiag_repeat] with identical call stack\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[55.017249, "o", "    The database experienced three internal errors (incidents 10193, 10194, 10195) within 10 seconds of each other. All share the exact same call stack originating from `dbkeTestFlowKGE_ORA` and `dbkeTest`. The presence of `dbkeTest` suggests this may be a kernel test flow or diagnostic probe rather than a standard user-session bug, but the recurrence and internal error code warrant investigation to rule out a known bug in the 23.26.3.0.0 version.\r\r\n"]
[55.445964, "o", "    \u001b[32m\u001b[1mproof\u001b[0m \u001b[35mev_f634f0007d\u001b[0m: \"ORA 600 [autodiag_repeat]: 3 incident(s)\"\r\r\n"]
[55.567838, "o", "    \u001b[32m\u001b[1mproof\u001b[0m \u001b[35mev_b2f7fac54c\u001b[0m: \"first application frame: dbkeTestFlowKGE_ORA [rdbms_dde]\"\r\r\n"]
[55.701494, "o", "    \u001b[32m\u001b[1mproof\u001b[0m \u001b[35mev_a025daa066\u001b[0m: \"identical code path in every incident: dbkeTestFlowKGE_ORA (3/3), dbkeTest (3/3)\"\r\r\n"]
[55.85494, "o", "    \u001b[36mnext:\u001b[0m Search My Oracle Support for ORA-00600 [autodiag_repeat] with frame dbkeTestFlowKGE_ORA\r\r\n"]
[56.000831, "o", "    \u001b[36mnext:\u001b[0m Verify if `dbkeTest` is an expected diagnostic probe in this version or a known bug\r\r\n"]
[56.14205, "o", " 2. \u001b[33m[warning/contributing]\u001b[0m \u001b[1mBackground process priority elevation failures (LGWR, VKTM)\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[56.278934, "o", "    The database failed to elevate the priority of LGWR and VKTM processes due to 'Operation not permitted'. This indicates a potential OS-level restriction (e.g., cgroups, systemd limits, or container permissions) that may affect database performance and stability, particularly under load. The error 'Dism(128)' suggests a Discrete Memory Allocator issue or OS permission mismatch.\r\r\n"]
[56.653042, "o", "    \u001b[32m\u001b[1mproof\u001b[0m \u001b[35mev_b71113542f\u001b[0m: \"Failed to elevate LGWR's priority from 0 to 1, policy 5\"\r\r\n"]
[56.786451, "o", "    \u001b[32m\u001b[1mproof\u001b[0m \u001b[35mev_11e2f29860\u001b[0m: \"Failed to elevate VKTM's priority from 0 to 1, policy 5\"\r\r\n"]
[56.920109, "o", "    \u001b[36mnext:\u001b[0m Check OS cgroup or systemd resource limits for the Oracle user\r\r\n"]
[57.045267, "o", "    \u001b[36mnext:\u001b[0m Verify if the database is running in a container with restricted CPU/IO priorities\r\r\n"]
[57.186481, "o", " 3. \u001b[36m[info/observation]\u001b[0m \u001b[1mORA-00600 [autodiag_probe] during startup\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[57.304758, "o", "    An earlier incident (10191) logged an ORA-00600 [autodiag_probe] error. This is typically a diagnostic probe used by the database to test AutoDiag functionality. While often benign, it confirms that the AutoDiag subsystem was active and generating internal errors during the startup window.\r\r\n"]
[57.607111, "o", "    \u001b[32m\u001b[1mproof\u001b[0m \u001b[35mev_ef989cb40d\u001b[0m: \"ORA-00600: internal error code, arguments: [autodiag_probe], [0], [0]\"\r\r\n"]
[57.751667, "o", "    \u001b[36mnext:\u001b[0m Confirm if autodiag_probe is expected in this environment\r\r\n"]
[57.873024, "o", "\r\r\n"]
[59.742001, "o", "\u001b[1mDismissed (6):\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[59.820548, "o", "\u001b[2m - JIT: pid <n> requesting stop x3: Routine JIT compiler activity during startup/shutdown, suppressed as noise.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[59.977953, "o", "\u001b[2m - Opening pdb with Resource Manager plan: DEFAULT_PLAN x2: Expected behavior when opening a PDB with a default plan.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[60.139086, "o", "\u001b[2m - Resize operation completed for file# <n>: Successful datafile resize, not an error.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[60.275644, "o", "\u001b[2m - Stopping background process CJQ0/MMNL: Normal background process lifecycle events.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[60.410655, "o", "\u001b[2m - Completed: Pluggable database FREEPDB1 closed services=None: Normal PDB close operation.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[60.551564, "o", "\u001b[2m - NMON services are only available for Exadata and OCI: Informational message about platform-specific features, not an error.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[60.719559, "o", "\r\r\n"]
[62.588867, "o", "\u001b[1mSuggested actions:\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[62.670242, "o", " - Package the incidents (10193, 10194, 10195) using ADRCI IPS for analysis by Oracle Support if the issue persists or is reproducible.\r\r\n"]
[62.845966, "o", " - Review the OS configuration for CPU/IO priority limits (cgroups, systemd) to resolve the 'Set Priority Failed' errors for LGWR and VKTM.\r\r\n"]
[63.024628, "o", " - Check the current Release Update (RU) for Oracle 23.26.3.0.0 to see if a patch for ORA-00600 [autodiag_repeat] with frame dbkeTestFlowKGE_ORA is available.\r\r\n"]
[63.21825, "o", "\r\r\n"]
[65.086958, "o", "\u001b[1mOpen questions:\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[65.166113, "o", " - Is `dbkeTestFlowKGE_ORA` a known diagnostic probe or a bug in version 23.26.3.0.0?\r\r\n"]
[65.301695, "o", " - What OS-level restrictions are preventing priority elevation for LGWR and VKTM?\r\r\n"]
[65.435593, "o", " - Are these incidents reproducible on restart, or were they one-off startup artifacts?\r\r\n"]
[65.574426, "o", "\r\r\n"]
[67.444659, "o", "\u001b[1mEvidence considered: 13 items (5 critical, 2 warning, 6 info); noise suppressed: 10 entries in 7 signatures; alert records seen 50\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
